'''trellis''' (trel′is), ''v. t.'' [< ''trellis'', ''n.''] '''1.''' To furnish with trellises or trellis-work; especially, to support or train on trellises: as, to ''trellis'' a vine. ''Bailey'', 1727.

{{smaller block|The rich moulding of masques and flowers and fruit . . . shone out amid the ''trellised'' trees.
